Windows CE 5.0: the SH4 kernel's loader accepts SH3 and SH3DSP executables
and DLLs (Pocket PC 2000 / CE 3.0 binaries: Math Xpander, mfcce300.dll).
loader.c's CPU-type chain has cases for SH3, MIPS and ARMV4I only, so on SH4
every foreign machine type is ERROR_BAD_EXE_FORMAT. SH-3 user-mode code is a
subset of SH-4 and uses software floating point (see SRC\APPS\SH3CRT for the
calling-convention side). Same change as loader-sh3-images.patch for CE 6.0.

Apply to %_WINCEROOT%\PRIVATE\WINCEOS\COREOS\NK\KERNEL\loader.c (the 2014
update rollup; the sources are CRLF, use --ignore-whitespace), then
`build -c` in that directory (nkmain.lib, nknocomp.lib, nkprof.lib) and a
Sysgen of the OS design so that nk.lib and kern.exe pick the new library.

--- a/PRIVATE/WINCEOS/COREOS/NK/KERNEL/loader.c
+++ b/PRIVATE/WINCEOS/COREOS/NK/KERNEL/loader.c
@@ -2537,6 +2537,12 @@
         if (!bIgnoreCPU && !e32ptr->e32_unit[14].rva && (e32ptr->e32_cpu != THISCPUID)) {
 #ifdef SH3
             if ((e32ptr->e32_cpu != IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_SH3DSP) || !SH3DSP)
                 return ERROR_BAD_EXE_FORMAT;
+#elif defined(SH4)
+            // CLASSPAD: SH-3 code runs on the SH-4 (user mode, software
+            // floating point): Pocket PC 2000 binaries load as they are
+            if ((e32ptr->e32_cpu != IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_SH3) && (e32ptr->e32_cpu != IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_SH3DSP))
+                return ERROR_BAD_EXE_FORMAT;
 #elif defined(MIPS)
             if ((e32ptr->e32_cpu != IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_MIPS16) || !IsMIPS16Supported)
                 return ERROR_BAD_EXE_FORMAT;
